{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Before a king ruled.</b> Before Moses, who was king in Israel, as it is written: 'And there was a king in Jeshurun' — on account of his having delivered Israel. And one should not explain it of Saul, for it is written in Josippon that these kings — close to forty kings named one after another — ruled before David, whereas here there are only eight, and from Abraham to Saul there are fourteen generations for the children of Israel. But when David ruled, he took the kingship from Edom, as it is written: 'And he placed governors in Edom, and all Edom became servants to David' — and so you find in Chronicles."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:35.137388537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}